+## Addendum — Desktop focus mode (explicit toggle + hover-reveal)
+
+**Date:** 2026-07-30 · **Status:** implemented · Trello: [#136](https://trello.com/c/wwxdYFNn/136-allow-focus-mode) · Branch: `feature/136-desktop-focus-mode`
+
+### Summary
+
+Mobile and tablet already hide Nav + the recitation bar on the reader (tap-background toggle,
+all addenda above). This adds the same panel-hiding to desktop (≥1367px, the "Desktop Reading
+Group" band) via an explicit toggle button in `Nav` plus hover-reveal — desktop has no
+tap-background convention and a mouse click risks conflicting with text selection, so the
+trigger mechanism differs by platform even though the underlying fixed/hidden CSS and
+`overlayVisible` state are reused as-is. See [ADR 0034](../architecture/adr/0034-desktop-focus-mode-hover-reveal.md)
+for why the click-toggle guard must NOT simply follow `isOverlayMode`.
+
+Explicitly **out of scope**: hiding the OS status bar (clock/battery/signal) on mobile/tablet.
+No web standard supports this in iOS Safari (`requestFullscreen()` has no non-video support
+there); an Android/desktop-only partial implementation was rejected as inconsistent. Deferred to
+a future ticket if wanted.
+
+### Decision Tree
+
+| Condition | Nav / recitation-bar behavior |
+|---|---|
+| Desktop (≥1367px), focus mode OFF (default) | Static, always visible — unchanged from today |
+| Desktop (≥1367px), focus mode ON, not hovering top hotzone / Nav | Fixed overlay, hidden (`-translate-y-full`, bar follows via existing sync) |
+| Desktop (≥1367px), focus mode ON, hovering top hotzone or over the revealed Nav | Fixed overlay, revealed |
+| Desktop (≥1367px), focus mode ON, cursor leaves Nav | Hides immediately |
+| Desktop, non-pages route | Static, always visible; toggle button not rendered |
+| Tablet/mobile (existing) | Unchanged — tap-background toggle untouched |
+| Click reader background on desktop | No-op — click-guard stays `isMobile \|\| isTablet`, never extended to desktop-focus |
+| Desktop window ≥1367px wide but <800px tall | Toggle still available; recitation bar keeps its existing full-width bottom-edge form (Desktop Reading Group's floating-card layout doesn't kick in, independent gate) |
+
+### Verified Test Cases
+
+| Scenario | Expected |
+|---|---|
+| Load `/pages/N` on desktop (≥1367px), first visit | Focus mode off, Nav + bar static, matches today |
+| Click focus-mode toggle in Nav | Focus mode on; Nav + bar immediately hide (fixed, translated off-screen) |
+| Move mouse to top hotzone while focus mode on | Nav (and synced bar) slide into view |
+| Move mouse off Nav, away from top | Nav + bar hide immediately |
+| Click the toggle again (visible via hover) | Focus mode off; Nav + bar return to static, always-visible |
+| Click/select Quran text on desktop, focus mode on or off | No effect on overlay state — no click-toggle guard fires for desktop |
+| Reload the page after enabling focus mode | Focus mode still on (persisted) |
+| Resize browser from 1400px to 1200px (into tablet band) while focus mode is on | Desktop `isOverlayMode` condition drops out; tablet's own tap-toggle condition takes over — no dual-trigger conflict, `overlayVisible` state carries over harmlessly |
+| Narrow desktop window (≥1367px wide, 700px tall) | Toggle still works; bar stays full-width bottom-edge (unaffected by the ≥800px Reading Group gate) |
+| Click a Quran word on desktop, focus mode on | Mark modal still opens (regression caught in review — see below) |
+| Navigate to a non-reader desktop route (e.g. home) after enabling focus mode | Hover hotzone does not mount there (regression caught in review — see below) |
+
+### Files to Change
+
+- **NEW `app/hooks/use-is-desktop-up.ts`** — width-only hook, `(min-width: 1367px)`, mirrors `use-is-tablet.ts`/`use-is-lg-up.ts` structure (SSR-safe, initializes `false`).
+- **`app/contexts/NavOverlayContext.tsx`** — add `desktopFocusEnabled` state (`useState`, initialized from `localStorage` key `desktopFocusMode` via an isomorphic layout effect — matching this same context's `isDesktopUp`/`isTablet`/`isMobile` pre-paint pattern so a returning user doesn't see Nav flash visible for a frame), `toggleDesktopFocus()` (flips + persists), and `isDesktopUp` via the new hook. Extend `isOverlayMode` to `((isMobile || isTablet) || (isDesktopUp && desktopFocusEnabled)) && isOnPagesRoute`. Also expose a second, narrower `isTouchOverlayMode = (isMobile || isTablet) && isOnPagesRoute` — the original pre-desktop meaning of `isOverlayMode` — for consumers that assume overlay mode implies a touch device (see review fix below). Export `desktopFocusEnabled`, `toggleDesktopFocus`, and `isTouchOverlayMode` from the context.
+- **`app/components/nav/Nav.tsx`** — new icon button in the trailing cluster (alongside `SharedMushafLink`/`MarksLink`/`SettingsSidebar`), rendered only when `isOnPagesRoute && isDesktopUp`, calling `toggleDesktopFocus()`. Icon reflects state (e.g. `Maximize2`/`Minimize2` from `lucide-react`).
+- **`app/components/nav/Nav.tsx`** — add a thin fixed top hotzone element (e.g. `h-2 fixed top-0 inset-x-0 z-50`), rendered only when `isOverlayMode && isDesktopUp` (not just `isDesktopUp && desktopFocusEnabled` — the latter is missing the `/pages/` route check that `isOverlayMode` already folds in; see review fix below), `onMouseEnter` sets `overlayVisible = true` (new context setter, or reuse a broadened `toggleOverlay`/add `showOverlay()`). Nav's root element gets `onMouseLeave` calling `hideOverlay()` (re-add a hide-only setter; the auto-hide-timer version was removed in an earlier addendum but the underlying setter shape can be reused) — gated to fire only when `isDesktopUp` so it doesn't interfere with tablet/mobile's tap-driven `overlayVisible`.
+- **`app/contexts/NavOverlayContext.tsx`** — `toggleOverlay()` itself gains the explicit `isMobile || isTablet` guard (in addition to its existing `isOverlayMode` check), so every call site — currently just `ReaderPager`'s background `onClick` — inherits the platform restriction with no per-callsite duplication.
+- **`app/components/QuranSafha.tsx`** — reads `isTouchOverlayMode` (not `isOverlayMode`) from `useNavOverlay()` and passes it as the `isOverlayMode` prop down to `QuranLine`/`QuranWord`. Review fix, see below.
+- **`app/globals.css`** — inside the existing `@media (min-width:1367px) and (min-height:800px)` block: add `.fq-recitation-bar-reader.translate-y-full { transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(100%); }`. Discovered during implementation: the shared `translate-y-full` Tailwind utility (also used by the mobile/tablet full-width bar) sets `transform: translateY(100%)` alone, which would otherwise replace — not compose with — this block's `translateX(-50%)` centering rule, animating a diagonal slide instead of a vertical one the first time desktop focus mode actually hides the floating bar. The two-class selector out-specifies the utility's one-class selector, so no `!important` is needed.
+
+### Bug fixes — found in code review before ship
+
+1. **Desktop word-click silently stopped opening the mark modal once desktop focus mode was on.** `QuranSafha.tsx` already threaded `isOverlayMode` down to `QuranWord` for click-vs-long-press gesture disambiguation (a pre-existing mobile/tablet mechanism: overlay mode suppresses the plain click handler in favor of a 500ms long-press, since a short tap toggles the nav instead). Widening `isOverlayMode` to include desktop-focus-on meant `QuranWord`'s `if (isOverlayMode) return;` guard now also fired on desktop — but desktop has no long-press equivalent (no touch events), so the click became a dead no-op with no other path to the mark modal. **Fix:** `NavOverlayContext` exposes `isTouchOverlayMode` (mobile/tablet only, the original meaning); `QuranSafha` now passes that instead of the broadened `isOverlayMode`. `isOverlayMode` itself is unchanged and still correctly drives the Nav/recitation-bar CSS. See ADR 0034's updated Consequences section.
+2. **Hover hotzone rendered on every desktop route, not just the reader.** The hotzone's render guard was `isDesktopUp && desktopFocusEnabled`, omitting the `/pages/` route check — once a user had ever enabled desktop focus mode, an invisible fixed `h-2` strip stayed mounted app-wide (home, settings, marks, etc.), and hovering it there silently mutated shared `overlayVisible` state for no visible reason. `showOverlay`/`hideOverlay` had the same gap. **Fix:** hotzone guard is now `isOverlayMode && isDesktopUp` (equivalent to the intended `isDesktopUp && desktopFocusEnabled && isOnPagesRoute`, since `isDesktopUp` and `isTablet`/`isMobile` are mutually exclusive by width); `showOverlay`/`hideOverlay` both add an explicit `isOnPagesRoute` check alongside their existing `isDesktopUp`/`desktopFocusEnabled` checks.
+3. **`desktopFocusEnabled`'s mount-time localStorage read used a plain `useEffect`**, resolving a tick after `isDesktopUp`/`isTablet`/`isMobile` (which use an isomorphic layout effect specifically to avoid a pre-paint flash) — a returning desktop user with focus mode already on would see Nav pop visible for a frame before snapping hidden. **Fix:** switched to the same isomorphic-layout-effect pattern as the other hooks in this context.
+
+**Noted, not a bug:** `PlansWidget` (the floating "Today's Plans" button) already reads the shared `isOverlayMode`/`overlayVisible` to mirror Nav's show/hide, unrelated to this ticket. Because `isOverlayMode` now also goes true for desktop-focus-on, enabling the new toggle makes this button hide/reveal along with Nav on desktop too. This is consistent with the deliberate "reuse the existing overlay mechanism" decision made during planning (RecitationPlayerBar already did the same automatically) rather than an oversight — recorded here since it wasn't spelled out explicitly before.
+
+### Constraints
+
+- Do not derive the click-to-toggle guard from `isOverlayMode` alone — `toggleOverlay()` must check platform (`isMobile || isTablet`) explicitly, per ADR 0034. Keep the guard centralized in `toggleOverlay()`, not duplicated at each call site.
+- `isDesktopUp` is width-only (≥1367px) and must NOT incorporate the Desktop Reading Group's ≥800px-tall gate — the two are deliberately independent (see Decision Tree, last row).
+- Reuse the existing `overlayVisible` state and CSS (`-translate-y-full` / `transition-transform`) for desktop — do not introduce a second visibility flag or a parallel CSS mechanism.
+- Persist `desktopFocusEnabled` in `localStorage`, matching the existing `quranSafhaView` pattern (read once at mount via isomorphic layout effect, write on every toggle).
+- No auto-hide timer on hover-reveal — hide fires only on `mouseleave`, immediately, mirroring the "explicit toggle only" decision already made for tablet/mobile's tap-reveal (no timer there either).
+- Do not attempt OS status-bar hiding (Fullscreen API or otherwise) as part of this addendum — explicitly deferred, see Summary.
+- Any new consumer of `NavOverlayContext` must choose `isOverlayMode` (broad, CSS-visibility use cases) vs `isTouchOverlayMode` (narrow, touch-gesture-disambiguation use cases) deliberately — do not assume `isOverlayMode` implies a touch context, per the word-click bug above.
+
+### What NOT to Do
+
+- Do not widen the background-click gesture to desktop under cover of widening `isOverlayMode` — this was evaluated and explicitly rejected (accidental-selection risk with a mouse).
+- Do not gate the desktop toggle button or hotzone on the Reading Group's ≥800px-tall condition — focus mode must remain available on shorter desktop windows too.
+- Do not add a Fullscreen-API-based status-bar hide for Android only while leaving iOS unmentioned — the decision was to defer the whole feature, not ship a partial/inconsistent version silently.
+- Do not pass the broad `isOverlayMode` to `QuranWord`/`QuranLine` for gesture disambiguation — use `isTouchOverlayMode`.
+- Do not gate the hover hotzone or `showOverlay`/`hideOverlay` on `isDesktopUp && desktopFocusEnabled` alone — always fold in the `/pages/` route check (via `isOverlayMode` or an explicit `isOnPagesRoute`).
+
+### Decisions Made
+
+- Desktop trigger: explicit Nav toggle button + hover-reveal (top hotzone + Nav `mouseleave`) — not the tap-background gesture used by tablet/mobile.
+- Desktop focus-mode scope: ≥1367px only (matches the existing tablet cutoff at 1366px exactly, no gap/overlap).
+- Preference persists in `localStorage`, same pattern as `quranSafhaView`.
+- Hide-on-mouseleave is immediate, no delay.
+- OS status-bar hiding is out of scope for this ticket; a follow-up ticket should be filed if wanted, scoped explicitly to Android/desktop given iOS Safari's Fullscreen API limitation.
+- `isOverlayMode` (broad) and `isTouchOverlayMode` (narrow, touch-only) are both exposed from `NavOverlayContext` going forward — a deliberate split made in review to avoid future consumers re-making the word-click mistake.

